Task 1: Configure Kubernetes Taints and Tolerations for HA
Subtask 1.1: Understanding Taints and Tolerations
Taints and tolerations work together to ensure that VMs are scheduled appropriately across nodes and can handle node-specific conditions.

Taints: Applied to nodes to repel certain pods/VMs
Tolerations: Applied to VMs to allow them to be scheduled on tainted nodes
Subtask 1.2: Examine Current Node Status
First, let's examine the current state of our cluster nodes:

# List all nodes in the cluster
oc get nodes

# Check node details and taints
oc describe nodes
Subtask 1.3: Apply Taints to Nodes
We'll apply taints to simulate different node conditions and prepare for HA scenarios:

# Apply a taint to simulate a node under maintenance
oc adm taint nodes worker-1 maintenance=true:NoSchedule

# Apply a taint for dedicated VM workloads
oc adm taint nodes worker-2 dedicated=vm-workload:NoSchedule

# Verify taints have been applied
oc describe node worker-1 | grep -i taint
oc describe node worker-2 | grep -i taint
Subtask 1.4: Create a VM with Tolerations
Create a VM configuration that includes tolerations to handle tainted nodes:

# Create file: ha-vm-with-tolerations.yaml
apiVersion: kubevirt.io/v1
kind: VirtualMachine
metadata:
  name: ha-vm-tolerations
  namespace: default
spec:
  running: true
  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        kubevirt.io/vm: ha-vm-tolerations
    spec:
      tolerations:
      - key: "dedicated"
        operator: "Equal"
        value: "vm-workload"
        effect: "NoSchedule"
      - key: "maintenance"
        operator: "Equal"
        value: "true"
        effect: "NoSchedule"
        tolerationSeconds: 300
      domain:
        devices:
          disks:
          - name: containerdisk
            disk:
              bus: virtio
          - name: cloudinitdisk
            disk:
              bus: virtio
          interfaces:
          - name: default
            masquerade: {}
        machine:
          type: ""
        resources:
          requests:
            memory: 1Gi
            cpu: 1
      networks:
      - name: default
        pod: {}
      volumes:
      - name: containerdisk
        containerDisk:
          image: quay.io/kubevirt/cirros-container-disk-demo
      - name: cloudinitdisk
        cloudInitNoCloud:
          userDataBase64: SGkuXG4=
Apply the VM configuration:

# Create the VM with tolerations
oc apply -f ha-vm-with-tolerations.yaml

# Verify VM creation and scheduling
oc get vms
oc get vmis
oc describe vmi ha-vm-tolerations
Subtask 1.5: Test Toleration Behavior
Verify that the VM can be scheduled on tainted nodes:

# Check which node the VM is running on
oc get vmi ha-vm-tolerations -o wide

# Verify the VM is tolerating the taints
oc describe vmi ha-vm-tolerations | grep -A 10 -i toleration
Task 2: Set VM Affinity Rules
Subtask 2.1: Understanding VM Affinity
VM affinity rules control how VMs are distributed across nodes:

Node Affinity: Controls which nodes VMs can be scheduled on
Pod Anti-Affinity: Ensures VMs are spread across different nodes
Pod Affinity: Groups related VMs on the same or nearby nodes
Subtask 2.2: Label Nodes for Affinity Rules
First, let's label our nodes to create logical groups:

# Label nodes with zones for affinity rules
oc label node worker-1 zone=zone-a
oc label node worker-2 zone=zone-b
oc label node worker-3 zone=zone-c

# Label nodes with hardware types
oc label node worker-1 hardware=ssd
oc label node worker-2 hardware=nvme
oc label node worker-3 hardware=ssd

# Verify labels
oc get nodes --show-labels
Subtask 2.3: Create VM with Node Affinity
Create a VM that prefers to run on nodes with SSD storage:

# Create file: ha-vm-node-affinity.yaml
apiVersion: kubevirt.io/v1
kind: VirtualMachine
metadata:
  name: ha-vm-node-affinity
  namespace: default
spec:
  running: true
  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        kubevirt.io/vm: ha-vm-node-affinity
        app: database
    spec:
      affinity:
        nodeAffinity:
          preferredDuringSchedulingIgnoredDuringExecution:
          - weight: 100
            preference:
              matchExpressions:
              - key: hardware
                operator: In
                values:
                - ssd
          requiredDuringSchedulingIgnoredDuringExecution:
            nodeSelectorTerms:
            - matchExpressions:
              - key: zone
                operator: In
                values:
                - zone-a
                - zone-b
                - zone-c
      domain:
        devices:
          disks:
          - name: containerdisk
            disk:
              bus: virtio
        machine:
          type: ""
        resources:
          requests:
            memory: 1Gi
            cpu: 1
      volumes:
      - name: containerdisk
        containerDisk:
          image: quay.io/kubevirt/cirros-container-disk-demo
Apply the configuration:

# Create the VM with node affinity
oc apply -f ha-vm-node-affinity.yaml

# Verify scheduling
oc get vmi ha-vm-node-affinity -o wide
Subtask 2.4: Create VMs with Anti-Affinity Rules
Create multiple VMs that should be distributed across different nodes:

# Create file: ha-vm-anti-affinity.yaml
apiVersion: kubevirt.io/v1
kind: VirtualMachine
metadata:
  name: ha-vm-web-1
  namespace: default
spec:
  running: true
  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        kubevirt.io/vm: ha-vm-web-1
        app: web-server
        tier: frontend
    spec:
      affinity:
        podAntiAffinity:
          requiredDuringSchedulingIgnoredDuringExecution:
          - labelSelector:
              matchExpressions:
              - key: app
                operator: In
                values:
                - web-server
            topologyKey: kubernetes.io/hostname
      domain:
        devices:
          disks:
          - name: containerdisk
            disk:
              bus: virtio
        machine:
          type: ""
        resources:
          requests:
            memory: 512Mi
            cpu: 500m
      volumes:
      - name: containerdisk
        containerDisk:
          image: quay.io/kubevirt/cirros-container-disk-demo
---
apiVersion: kubevirt.io/v1
kind: VirtualMachine
metadata:
  name: ha-vm-web-2
  namespace: default
spec:
  running: true
  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        kubevirt.io/vm: ha-vm-web-2
        app: web-server
        tier: frontend
    spec:
      affinity:
        podAntiAffinity:
          requiredDuringSchedulingIgnoredDuringExecution:
          - labelSelector:
              matchExpressions:
              - key: app
                operator: In
                values:
                - web-server
            topologyKey: kubernetes.io/hostname
      domain:
        devices:
          disks:
          - name: containerdisk
            disk:
              bus: virtio
        machine:
          type: ""
        resources:
          requests:
            memory: 512Mi
            cpu: 500m
      volumes:
      - name: containerdisk
        containerDisk:
          image: quay.io/kubevirt/cirros-container-disk-demo
Apply the anti-affinity configuration:

# Create VMs with anti-affinity rules
oc apply -f ha-vm-anti-affinity.yaml

# Verify VMs are on different nodes
oc get vmi -l app=web-server -o wide
Subtask 2.5: Verify Affinity Rule Enforcement
Check that the affinity rules are working correctly:

